  "title": "Intraoperative ECoG strip and subthalamic LFP during grip-force in Parkinson's disease (Merk et al. 2022)",
  "description": "Intraoperative electrocorticography (ECoG) from subdural strips over sensorimotor cortex and subthalamic nucleus local field potentials (STN LFP) recorded during a grip-force task in 16 people with Parkinson's disease undergoing DBS lead implantation. The dataset contains 73 runs, resampled to 1 kHz, with grip-force traces and MNI-space electrode locations. It supports comparison of cortical and subthalamic signals for movement decoding.",
  "methods_description": "Recordings were made intraoperatively during bilateral STN-DBS lead implantation using a Grapevine neural interface processor (Ripple). Signals were filtered at 0.3-7.5 kHz, digitised at 30 kHz and resampled to 1 kHz. ECoG was recorded from temporary subdural strips and STN LFP from four-contact DBS leads (Medtronic 3389). Contacts were localised from MRI, CT and fluoroscopy and transformed into MNI space (Lead-DBS).",
